Urza turns every artifact you control into a blue mana. Not artifacts that tap for mana — ALL of them: the Construct token he brings with him, Clues, Baubles, Equipment, even Sol Ring after you have already tapped it for its own mana would not work, but everything untapped does. That one line is why this deck's mana is effectively its board, and why an untap effect is the same thing as a ritual.

# The commander
Urza, Lord High Artificer :: arrives with a Construct that is as big as your artifact count, taps any untapped artifact for {U}, and his {5} ability exiles the top card of your library and lets you play it free.
Tapping an artifact for Urza's mana uses it up. You cannot tap Sol Ring for {C}{C} and then tap it again for Urza — pick one. That is the main thing people get wrong.
The {5} ability is the deck's engine once mana is unlimited: shuffle, exile, cast free, repeat until you find the kill.
Lightning Greaves :: haste so the {5} ability works immediately, and shroud against the removal that follows him.

# The infinite mana
Isochron Scepter :: imprint Dramatic Reversal. {2} and a tap copies it, untapping every nonland permanent you control. If those permanents tap for three or more with Urza out — and they always do — the loop pays for itself forever.
Dramatic Reversal :: the other half, and a fine card on its own for a big Urza turn.
Basalt Monolith :: taps for three, untaps for three. On its own that is nothing; with either card below it is unlimited colourless mana.
Power Artifact :: enchanted artifact's activated abilities cost {2} less. Basalt Monolith now untaps for {1} and taps for three.
Forensic Gadgeteer :: the same reduction across ALL your artifacts, and it makes a Clue on every artifact spell.
Rings of Brighthearth :: copies any nonmana activated ability for {2}, including Urza's {5}, Tezzeret's minus and Walking Ballista's ping.

# What unlimited mana buys
Walking Ballista :: {4} for a counter, remove a counter to ping. With infinite mana it kills the table, and with none it is still a flexible removal creature.
Urza, Lord High Artificer :: the {5} ability, over and over, casting your entire library for free.
Whir of Invention :: instant speed, improvise, fetches any artifact — including the missing combo piece.
Reshape :: the sorcery version, tutoring straight onto the battlefield.
Transmute Artifact :: trades a big artifact for whatever you need.
Tezzeret the Seeker :: the minus finds any artifact onto the battlefield; the plus untaps two.

# Winning without the combo
This is the answer to "does it just run out of gas" — it does not, and it has a fair kill.
Cyberdrive Awakener :: every noncreature artifact becomes a 4/4 AND they all fly. On a board of twelve artifacts that is a lethal alpha strike from nowhere.
Tezzeret the Seeker :: the ultimate does the same for a turn.
The Construct token Urza brings with him is as big as your artifact count — by turn six that is eight or ten power on a single body, and Cyberdrive Awakener gives it flying.
Mechanized Production :: enchant an artifact you have several copies of — or one that copies itself — and it makes another every upkeep. At eight with the same name, you simply win.
Sai, Master Thopterist :: a flying Thopter for every artifact spell, and a sacrifice outlet that draws.

# Card flow
The One Ring :: a full turn of protection, then it draws an escalating pile — the single best card in the deck for a grindy game.
Mystic Forge :: cast artifacts and colourless spells straight off the top of your library. With Sensei's Divining Top it never stops.
Sensei's Divining Top :: sets your draws, and it is an artifact that taps for {U} under Urza.
The Reality Chip :: attach it and you play everything off the top, lands included.
Padeem, Consul of Innovation :: your artifacts get hexproof — which answers the artifact removal this deck folds to — and it draws most upkeeps.
Rhystic Study :: their turns pay for yours.
Mystic Remora :: the best card in the deck on turns one through four.
Faerie Mastermind :: flash, flies, draws off the table's extra draws.
Emry, Lurker of the Loch :: nearly free, mills four, and recasts an artifact from your graveyard every turn.
Timetwister :: a fresh seven for everyone when you have emptied your hand.
Windfall :: the same, and it hits hardest when someone is hoarding.

# Making artifacts cheap
Etherium Sculptor :: artifact spells cost one less.
Foundry Inspector :: the second copy.
Sapphire Medallion :: the blue half.
Mox Opal :: metalcraft is immediate here.
Lotus Petal :: free, and it is an artifact for Urza before it is sacrificed.
Jeweled Amulet :: stores mana across turns.
Everflowing Chalice :: scales to whatever you have spare.
Mind Stone :: ramp early, a card later.
Thought Vessel :: mana and no maximum hand size, which matters with The One Ring.
Mishra's Bauble :: zero mana, an artifact, and a card next upkeep.
Urza's Bauble :: the same.

# Untaps, which are mana
Voltaic Key :: untap any artifact.
Manifold Key :: the same, and it makes a creature unblockable for the kill.
Unwinding Clock :: untaps every artifact during each opponent's untap step. With Urza that is a full extra pool of blue mana on all three of their turns.
Copy Artifact :: a second Basalt Monolith, Isochron Scepter or Mox Opal.
Phyrexian Metamorph :: a copy of the best artifact or creature on the board.

# Interaction
Counterspell :: the clean two-mana answer.
Mana Drain :: counter, and the mana pays for the combo turn.
Force of Negation :: free on their turn.
Pact of Negation :: free now, and the deck usually wins before the upkeep.
Flusterstorm :: nearly unbeatable in a counter war.
Swan Song :: one mana for a wrath or an enchantment.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: the same for anything noncreature.
Mental Misstep :: two life for their turn-one accelerant.
Mindbreak Trap :: free against a storm turn, and it exiles.
Muddle the Mixture :: a counterspell, or transmute for Isochron Scepter, Basalt Monolith or Power Artifact — all mana value two.
Solve the Equation :: any instant or sorcery, usually Dramatic Reversal.
Merchant Scroll :: any blue instant.
Fabricate :: any artifact, to hand.
Spellskite :: redirects the removal spell aimed at Urza for two life.
Chain of Vapor :: one mana to bounce anything.
Pongify :: one mana, kills anything.
Cyclonic Rift :: overloaded, the clear for a lethal artifact attack.
Hullbreaker Horror :: uncounterable, flash, and every spell afterwards bounces something.
Trinisphere :: a tax that hurts a fast table far more than a deck that generates its own mana.
Tormod's Crypt :: free graveyard hate that is also an artifact for Urza.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep cheap artifacts and a land. Mox Opal, Lotus Petal, Mishra's Bauble and Sol Ring all make Urza a turn-three play and immediately turn into mana once he lands.
Count Urza's mana correctly. Each untapped artifact is one blue, once. Tapping Sol Ring for its own two means it is no longer available for Urza — work out which use you need before you start.
Muddle the Mixture :: remember it transmutes for exactly two. Isochron Scepter, Basalt Monolith and Power Artifact are all two, so it is a tutor for whichever combo half you are missing.
Hold up interaction on the turn you go off. The deck's failure case is a single counterspell on Dramatic Reversal, and Force of Negation or Pact of Negation costs you nothing to keep available.
